{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Therefore I hated.</b> There are חיים in the sacred tongue that are an adjective in plural form, like חיים כולכם היום (Deuteronomy 5:3). And there are חיים that are a noun and not an adjective, like מות וחיים (death and life), and no singular form derives from it, like נעורים and זקונים and שלמים and מלואים, and others like them. And the חיים in this verse is an adjective."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:09.769979111Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}